1456
01:10:49,270 --> 01:10:52,540
It is, especially if you've got years and years of legacy content.

1457
01:10:52,680 --> 01:10:57,540
And I think a lot of people just try to migrate everything over as is.

1458
01:10:58,100 --> 01:11:01,150
But this is actually a good opportunity to do some screen cleaning, right?

1459
01:11:01,170 --> 01:11:01,930
Oh, absolutely.

1460
01:11:01,970 --> 01:11:04,230
Get rid of anything that's outdated, irrelevant.

1461
01:11:04,610 --> 01:11:08,770
Make sure the content you do keep aligns with your current goals and objectives.

1462
01:11:08,950 --> 01:11:10,100
Streamline that library.

1463
01:11:10,300 --> 01:11:10,780
Exactly.

1464
01:11:10,880 --> 01:11:15,920
And when you're creating new content, keep mobile accessibility top of mind.

1465
01:11:15,990 --> 01:11:17,330
So no more tiny fonts.

1466
01:11:17,390 --> 01:11:18,530
No more tiny fonts.

1467
01:11:18,610 --> 01:11:20,410
No more clunky navigation.

1468
01:11:20,430 --> 01:11:22,030
It's got to look good on a phone.

1469
01:11:22,340 --> 01:11:24,200
It's got to be easy to use on any device.

1470
01:11:24,240 --> 01:11:25,380
Make it seamless.

1471
01:11:25,440 --> 01:11:26,520
Make it enjoyable.

1472
01:11:26,700 --> 01:11:32,790
But even with the best content, the most user-friendly LMS, it's all for nothing if people don't actually use it.

1473
01:11:32,810 --> 01:11:33,230
You're right.

1474
01:11:33,390 --> 01:11:34,570
User adoption is key.

1475
01:11:34,670 --> 01:11:35,710
It's the make or break factor.

1476
01:11:36,010 --> 01:11:40,240
So how do you get people excited about a new learning platform?

1477
01:11:40,220 --> 01:11:43,270
I mean, it's not exactly the most glamorous thing in the world.

1478
01:11:43,480 --> 01:11:44,610
It's not like a new iPhone.

1479
01:11:44,830 --> 01:11:45,570
Right, exactly.

1480
01:11:45,770 --> 01:11:49,170
But there are ways to build that excitement to encourage adoption.

1481
01:11:49,410 --> 01:11:50,140
Okay, I'm listening.

1482
01:11:50,200 --> 01:11:56,020
One thing Mary mentioned that I thought was brilliant was involving employees in that selection process from the very beginning.

1483
01:11:56,280 --> 01:11:56,950
Oh, I like that.

1484
01:11:57,280 --> 01:11:58,480
Yeah, give them a voice.

1485
01:11:58,640 --> 01:12:02,290
Let them have a say in what features and functionality they want to see.

1486
01:12:02,330 --> 01:12:04,490
Make them feel like they're part of the decision.

1487
01:12:04,790 --> 01:12:06,650
Exactly, create that sense of ownership.

1488
01:12:06,670 --> 01:12:10,620
And once you've chosen an LMS, make sure you communicate those benefits clearly.

1489
01:12:10,760 --> 01:12:11,920
Sell it, sell it, sell it.

1490
01:12:12,220 --> 01:12:13,820
Yeah, show them what's in it for them.

1491
01:12:14,120 --> 01:12:16,790
And don't underestimate the power of training and support.

1492
01:12:17,030 --> 01:12:19,230
Right, make sure they know how to use the new system.

1493
01:12:19,290 --> 01:12:21,030
Give them the resources they need.

1494
01:12:21,290 --> 01:12:22,800
Be there to answer their questions.

1495
01:12:22,900 --> 01:12:25,140
Be patient, be supportive.

1496
01:12:25,320 --> 01:12:26,880
And what about gamification?

1497
01:12:27,770 --> 01:12:30,960
Mary talked about using things like badges and leaderboards.

1498
01:12:31,120 --> 01:12:32,340
Oh, I love gamification.

1499
01:12:32,460 --> 01:12:32,980
Make it fun.

1500
01:12:33,040 --> 01:12:34,020
Make it a competition.

1501
01:12:34,140 --> 01:12:36,750
A little friendly competition never hurt anybody.

1502
01:12:36,970 --> 01:12:37,490
Exactly.

1503
01:12:37,590 --> 01:12:42,950
It's a great way to motivate people, especially those who thrive on recognition and rewards.

1504
01:12:43,420 --> 01:12:50,270
But before we get too carried away with all the fun stuff, let's not forget about integration, especially with the HRIS system.

1505
01:12:50,690 --> 01:12:52,010
Oh, integration.

1506
01:12:52,050 --> 01:12:53,350
That's crucial.

1507
01:12:53,410 --> 01:12:54,430
It's got to be seamless, right?

1508
01:12:54,490 --> 01:12:54,790
It does.

1509
01:12:54,830 --> 01:12:56,840
You don't want that LMS to be an island.

1510
01:12:56,980 --> 01:12:57,350
Right.

1511
01:12:57,550 --> 01:12:58,790
Got to be part of the ecosystem.

1512
01:12:59,110 --> 01:12:59,850
It's all connected.

1513
01:13:00,710 --> 01:13:04,460
Integrating it with the HRIS allows for that seamless data flow.

1514
01:13:04,800 --> 01:13:09,230
You can track training records, certifications, skills, performance reviews, everything.

1515
01:13:09,250 --> 01:13:11,730
It's like having a 360-degree view of the employee.

1516
01:13:11,930 --> 01:13:12,680
Exactly.

1517
01:13:12,720 --> 01:13:18,590
And it helps you make better decisions about talent development, succession planning, compensation.

1518
01:13:18,720 --> 01:13:20,680
So it's not just about learning for learning's sake.

1519
01:13:21,140 --> 01:13:22,800
It's about connecting it to the bigger picture.

1520
01:13:23,050 --> 01:13:23,550
Absolutely.

1521
01:13:23,560 --> 01:13:26,850
It's about aligning those learning goals with the business goals.

1522
01:13:26,870 --> 01:13:31,820
And that brings us full circle to that key insight we've been talking about throughout this entire deep dive.

1523
01:13:31,980 --> 01:13:32,660
You got it.

1524
01:13:32,680 --> 01:13:40,190
Every tech decision we've discussed, from SD-WAN and AI to cloud migration and project management software, it all comes down to this.

1525
01:13:41,170 --> 01:13:42,550
How will it impact our people?

1526
01:13:42,580 --> 01:13:44,200
People first, technology second.

1527
01:13:44,320 --> 01:13:44,740
Exactly.

1528
01:13:44,940 --> 01:13:46,700
How will we bring them along on this journey?

1529
01:13:47,010 --> 01:13:49,690
How will we make sure it empowers them and doesn't replace them?

1530
01:13:49,710 --> 01:13:51,870
Those are the questions every leader should be asking themselves.

1531
01:13:52,190 --> 01:13:58,620
Because technology will always be evolving, but it's the human element that will always be at the heart of any successful business.

1532
01:13:59,000 --> 01:13:59,860
Couldn't agree more.

1533
01:13:59,880 --> 01:14:03,480
And that's what we've been exploring in this deep dive.

1534
01:14:04,090 --> 01:14:09,750
And I hope it's given you some food for thought as you navigate this exciting and something overwhelming world of business tech.

1535
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:15,220
Yeah, it's a lot to take in, but it's also incredibly exciting to think about all the possibilities.

1536
01:14:15,400 --> 01:14:15,740
It is.

1537
01:14:15,960 --> 01:14:17,760
And that's why we love doing these deep dives.

1538
01:14:17,820 --> 01:14:20,890
So thanks for joining us on this journey and we'll see you next time.
